{
  "id": "li-rinzel-closed-calcium-second-biology",
  "name": "Li-Rinzel closed-store calcium and receptor inactivation",
  "description": "IP3- and calcium-dependent release competes with saturating ER pumping and slow receptor inactivation. No plasma-membrane flux, spatial calcium waves or stochastic channel claims. Uses the documented Physiome parameters and initial C0.2,h0.8, with our explicit epsilon=0 closed-store specialization and constant total calcium2. Time is seconds: the source millisecond factors0.001 are removed consistently. Horizon200 and RK4step0.02 are illustrative verification choices. https://models.cellml.org/exposure/be7a891ac95b45c9b651f88821b6d2b4/li_rinzel_1994.cellml Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1994.1041",
  "reference": "Li and Rinzel (1994), Equations for InsP3 receptor-mediated intracellular calcium oscillations derived from a detailed kinetic model, J Theor Biol166:461-473. Physiome exposurebe7a891ac95b45c9b651f88821b6d2b4.",
